1
00:00:00,336 --> 00:00:05,474
The Dashboard — Hours, utilisation, budgets and approvals at a glance — and dashboards you build yourself.

2
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:11,792
Choose the period: this week, this month, the last three months, the year or all time.

3
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:21,930
Values or % switches the charts between hours and shares; Export saves the numbers to Excel.

4
00:00:22,677 --> 00:00:28,783
The filters narrow everything to one person, client, project or work order. You see only the people in your scope.

5
00:00:29,459 --> 00:00:36,464
The manager cockpit shows what needs you: approvals waiting, projects close to their budget, people over capacity and hours still in approval.

6
00:00:37,243 --> 00:00:42,852
Then the totals: all hours, Yellow client hours, Red company hours, and utilisation — the share of Yellow.

7
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:49,614
Below, the charts: hours over time, by client, plan against actual, sick and vacation days, expenses…

8
00:00:51,191 --> 00:00:56,806
You can build your own. + New dashboard starts an empty one; Customize changes the one you're on.

9
00:00:59,412 --> 00:01:05,957
Now every widget has buttons to move it, change its settings or remove it — and the bar has Rename, Duplicate, Reset and Delete.

10
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:09,285
+ Add widget offers ready-made widgets…

11
00:01:11,879 --> 00:01:16,748
…or Build your own from any measure, grouping and chart. Let's add Hours by project.

12
00:01:19,613 --> 00:01:25,045
It's added at the end. When you're happy, press Done — the dashboard is saved for you.

13
00:01:27,524 --> 00:01:31,709
See · narrow · build your own — More help: the Handbook → Dashboard.
